Spires, belfries, cupolas, domes, monuments, roof signs, water towers, observation towers, electrical transmission towers, silos, chimneys, smokestacks, elevators, conveyors, flag poles, mast, steeples, and windmills that exceed the height limitations for the district in which they are located, as outlined in the ordinance, require approval from the Glynn County Planning Commission. When considering an exception, the Planning Commission must consider the following factors:
